@thalheimer
title: August Thalheimer: analyse the crisis
subtitle: A theoretical report on the situation. · dev: kf_right_strength +4, kf_centre_dissent −3, adv_right_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if thalheimer_timer > 0 : [+ thalheimer_timer +] months before Thalheimer can act again. ?]
choose-if: thalheimer_timer = 0
on-arrival: thalheimer_timer = 3; kf_right_strength += 4; kf_centre_dissent -= 3; adv_right_last = time

Thalheimer writes the party its analysis: a crisis of the whole bourgeois order, and a party that must not mistake it for the revolution itself. The Centre, tired of slogans, is glad of a text.

@walcher
title: Jacob Walcher: win the unions
subtitle: Fractions in the factory councils and unions. · dev: workers_kpd +3×m, kf_right_strength +3, adv_right_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if walcher_timer > 0 : [+ walcher_timer +] months before Walcher can act again. ?]
choose-if: walcher_timer = 0
on-arrival: walcher_timer = 3; workers_kpd += 3*campaign_mult; kf_right_strength += 3; adv_right_last = time

Walcher knows the works councils and the metalworkers' branches, and the party's fractions are told to stay inside the unions and fight there. It is slow work, and it is the work that wins majorities.

@radek
title: Karl Radek: ask what Moscow thinks
subtitle: A letter to the Executive. · dev: trust +6, kf_right_strength +4, kf_left_dissent +3, adv_right_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if radek_timer > 0 : [+ radek_timer +] months before Radek can act again. ?]
choose-if: radek_timer = 0
on-arrival: radek_timer = 3; comintern_trust += 6; kf_right_strength += 4; kf_left_dissent += 3; adv_right_last = time

Radek writes to Moscow, in his own style, and tells Zinoviev what the Zentrale wishes to hear and the Executive wishes to be told. The Right is pleased that its case has a voice in Moscow. The Left suspects that Radek is saving himself.

@heckert
title: Fritz Heckert: work with the Saxon ministers
subtitle: A government of workers in Dresden. · dev: y23_unity +1, kf_left_dissent +2, workers_kpd +1×m, adv_right_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if heckert_timer > 0 : [+ heckert_timer +] months before Heckert can act again. ?]
choose-if: heckert_timer = 0
on-arrival: heckert_timer = 3; y23_unity += 1; kf_left_dissent += 2; workers_kpd += 1*campaign_mult; adv_right_last = time

Heckert, who will be a minister if there is a workers' government, works with the SPD ministers in Dresden on the control committees and the proletarian hundreds. It is concrete work and the Left calls it ministerialism.
